    "description": {
      "value": "<p data-start=\"1567\" data-end=\"1580\"><em data-start=\"1567\" data-end=\"1580\">(3rd Level)</em></p><p><strong>Noise:</strong> +1</p><p data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1697\">Once per scene, when an <strong data-start=\"1606\" data-end=\"1627\">Out of Compliance</strong> target violates a binding contract or established precedent, you may:</p><ul data-start=\"1699\" data-end=\"1788\"><li data-start=\"1699\" data-end=\"1749\"><p data-start=\"1701\" data-end=\"1749\">Force a reroll (taking the worse result), <strong data-start=\"1743\" data-end=\"1749\">or</strong></p></li><li data-start=\"1750\" data-end=\"1788\"><p data-start=\"1752\" data-end=\"1788\">Cause the target to lose its action.</p></li></ul><p data-start=\"1790\" data-end=\"1839\">This represents procedural enforcement\u2014not anger.</p><h3 data-start=\"1841\" data-end=\"1849\">Cost</h3><p data-start=\"1850\" data-end=\"1865\">Free (1/scene).</p><h3 data-start=\"1867\" data-end=\"1881\">Escalation</h3><p data-start=\"1882\" data-end=\"2006\">If paired with a Surge spend, the action loss cannot be mitigated by legendary or divine resistance (GM adjudicated).</p><h3 data-start=\"2008\" data-end=\"2020\">Pushback</h3><p data-start=\"2021\" data-end=\"2070\">Repeated public enforcement increases visibility.</p><p><em>Recosted 2026-08-23: this ability's earlier economy (Civic Charge / Strain / Resonance / Leverage / Administrative Pressure) is retired \u2014 everything now runs on Surge, Clarity, Noise, and the misfire ladder. The ability dialog's cost line is the truth; ledgers named here are narrative, GM-adjudicated, never a tracked pool.</em></p>",
